    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0451" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/375: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-20T13:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 20,
                                1923—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>56. Haskell left Greece March 19 for Anatolia on an American destroyer to take up
                    with Turkish authorities a proposal of Mr. Hoover<anchor n="7" xml:id="d219-f1"
                    /> relating to American relief for Turkish devastated regions on condition that
                    the Turks permit refugees in Greece to return to their homes in Turkey. This
                    matter is being kept confidential in Athens and is not known to the Greek
                    authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d219-f1" n="7" xml:id="d219-f1-content">
                <p>Chairman of the American Relief Administration.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
